UPDATE companies SET description='Scotchman Industries was founded in 1949 in Philip, South Dakota, where it continues to manufacture its full line of metal fabrication equipment. The company is now part of SMX Industrial Solutions, a group that also includes Steelmax Tools and Preston Eastin, broadening its portfolio while maintaining production in its original facility.

The company builds a complete range of American-made machinery for metal fabrication, including 14 models of hydraulic ironworkers from 45 to 150 tons, ferrous and non-ferrous cold saws in manual through fully automatic configurations, pipe notchers (manual, electric, and abrasive), hydraulic presses in 66-, 110-, and 176-ton capacities, measuring systems from manual to full-auto feed, as well as bandsaws, belt sanders, horizontal benders, and conveyor systems. Scotchman also produces tooling, accessories, and replacement parts, and operates an in-house blade sharpening service that typically returns high-speed steel blades within two business days.

Scotchman’s equipment is used by metal fabrication shops, manufacturers, and industrial operations across North America and beyond, as well as by educational programs such as high school welding and fabrication classes. Customers cited on the company’s site include a fabrication shop in Canada and Petty Welding in Knoxville, Tennessee.

Scotchman emphasizes that its ironworkers are 100% American-made and designed for decades of service, highlighting rugged construction, precision, and reliability as core differentiators. The SMX Industrial affiliation adds access to advanced welding mechanization and robotic positioning solutions, allowing the company to offer a more comprehensive fabrication toolkit.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hydraulic ironworker manufacturing", "Cold saw manufacturing (ferrous and non-ferrous)", "Pipe notcher manufacturing", "Hydraulic press manufacturing", "Measuring system manufacturing", "Bandsaw manufacturing", "Belt sander manufacturing", "Horizontal bender manufacturing", "Conveyor system manufacturing", "Tooling and accessory production", "Blade sharpening service", "Equipment financing", "Warranty and repair service", "Used equipment sales", "Onsite equipment demonstrations"], "industries": ["Metal fabrication", "Manufacturing", "Industrial operations", "Education (trade schools)"], "materials": ["Steel", "Structural steel", "Tubing", "Flat bar", "Angle iron", "Plate", "High-speed steel (HSS)"], "equipment": ["Ironworkers (45-150 ton)", "Cold saws (ferrous/non-ferrous, manual to fully automatic)", "Pipe notchers (manual, electric, abrasive)", "Hydraulic presses (66, 110, 176 ton)", "Measuring systems (manual, digital, semi-auto, full-auto)", "Bandsaws (SU-280-G)", "Belt sanders (DBS-3)", "Belt grinders (SG3)", "Horizontal benders (HB-31, HB-88)", "Conveyors (open, covered roller, solid)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "2 business days for HSS blade sharpening", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% American-made ironworkers produced in Philip, South Dakota", "In-house blade sharpening with two-business-day turnaround", "Free onsite equipment demonstrations", "Part of SMX Industrial Solutions for expanded fabrication solutions", "Comprehensive product line covering cutting, bending, punching, and measuring"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1949 in Philip, South Dakota -> db", "Headquarters Philip, South Dakota -> db, /about", "Part of SMX Industrial Solutions (with Steelmax Tools and Preston Eastin) -> /about", "14 ironworker models 45-150 ton -> /", "Cold saws ferrous/non-ferrous manual to fully automatic -> /", "Pipe notchers manual, electric, abrasive -> /", "Hydraulic presses 66, 110, 176 ton -> /", "Measuring systems manual to full-auto -> /", "Bandsaws, belt sanders, horizontal benders, conveyors -> /", "In-house blade sharpening 2 business days -> /", "Customers: fabrication shop Canada, Petty Welding Knoxville TN -> /", "100% American-made ironworkers -> /", "Languages English, Espa\u00f1ol, Portugu\u00eas -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are proud to say that our world-famous ironworkers are still made in small-town Philip, South Dakota, USA", "founded_year": "1949", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": ["English", "Espa\u00f1ol", "Portugu\u00eas"], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/scotchman-industries-inc/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='scotchman-industries-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Scott Jordan Furniture Inc. was founded in 1980 by Scott Jordan as a furniture repair shop on Atlantic Avenue in Brooklyn''s Boerum Hill neighborhood. The business began with recaning and reweaving chair seats, furniture repair, and restoration before expanding into custom solid-wood furniture production.

Today the company operates a factory workshop and showroom in the Brooklyn Navy Yard, where it designs and builds heirloom-quality sofa beds, bed frames, mattresses, and cabinetry using a hybrid of CAD/CAM-driven CNC cutting, 3D modeling, and traditional hand-finishing joinery techniques. The in-house team handles custom modifications, delivery, and installation throughout New York City, navigating tight urban spaces such as Manhattan apartments and Brooklyn brownstones.

The firm serves residential clients across the New York metro area and collaborates with upholstery partner American Leather on complex pieces. Its showroom displays over 25 floor models and full fabric libraries, allowing customers to experience materials and finishes firsthand.

Founder Scott Jordan emphasizes non-toxic, sustainable materials—sourcing Pennsylvania cherry, Ohio/Indiana walnut, Appalachian oak, and Eastern Linden from managed forests—and applies hand-rubbed natural oil and wax finishes. The company''s manufacturing paradigm shifted to full CAD/CAM in 1999, enabling one-at-a-time production with high customization for NYC interiors.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CAD/CAM design and manufacturing", "CNC cutting", "3D modeling", "Hand-finishing", "Traditional joinery (bed bolts)", "Custom furniture design", "Delivery and installation in NYC", "Furniture repair and restoration", "Recaning and reweaving chair seats", "Solid wood furniture manufacturing", "Custom modifications to existing designs", "Hybrid woodworking (digital + handcraft)"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Interior design for urban spaces", "Upholstery collaboration"], "materials": ["Pennsylvania cherry", "Walnut (Ohio/Indiana)", "Appalachian oak", "Eastern Linden", "Solid hardwoods", "Natural oil and wax finishes"], "equipment": ["CNC machinery", "Table saws", "Routers", "Shapers"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house delivery and installation team (no third-party contractors)", "Hybrid woodworking: CAD/CAM, CNC, and hand-finishing under one roof", "Factory showroom at Brooklyn Navy Yard for transparent production viewing", "Non-toxic, hand-rubbed natural oil and wax finishes on sustainably sourced hardwoods", "Expertise in NYC space constraints: narrow staircases, walk-ups, compact interiors"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1980 as furniture repair shop on Atlantic Avenue, Brooklyn -> /about-us", "Founder Scott Jordan -> /about-us", "Moved to Brooklyn Navy Yard workshop 1988, showroom 2020 -> /", "CAD adoption 1993, full CAD/CAM 1999 -> /", "Products: sofa beds, bed frames, mattresses, cabinetry -> /, /quality", "Processes: CAD/CAM, CNC cutting, 3D modeling, hand-finishing, traditional joinery -> /, /about-us", "In-house delivery/installation team -> /", "Materials: Pennsylvania cherry, walnut (Ohio/Indiana), Appalachian oak, Eastern Linden -> /", "Finishes: hand-rubbed natural oil and wax, non-toxic -> /, /quality", "Serves NYC metro area, Manhattan apartments, Brooklyn brownstones -> /, /about-us", "Collaboration with American Leather -> /about-us", "Showroom: 25+ floor models, fabric libraries -> /", "Sustainability: renewable, non-toxic materials from managed forests -> /", "One-at-a-time production with high customization -> /about-us", "Headquarters: Brooklyn, New York -> db, /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "The workshop grew and prospered always focusing on solid wood residential furniture.", "founded_year": "1980", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='scott-jordan-furniture-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SDI Sportswear, based in Salt Lake City, Utah, was founded in 1985 and is now in its thirty-eighth year. The company began by designing and decorating sportswear for ski resorts across the Western United States, including Colorado, California, and Utah.

Today the company operates a full-service art department, a screen-printing facility, and embroidery and appliqué production in-house. Services include custom screen-printed apparel, embroidered garments and accessories, promotional products for trade shows and giveaways, and graphic design and branding support. SDI also produces its own resort and golf sportswear lines and manufactures private-label brands for clients.

SDI serves ski and golf resorts, country clubs, and corporate clients across the United States and Canada. Corporate customers use the company''s screen printing and embroidery for event promotion and employee recognition programs, while resorts and clubs source custom sportswear and promotional items.

SDI emphasizes its in-house capabilities as a differentiator: the art department collaborates directly with screen-printing and embroidery production to maintain quality control and shorten lead times. The company highlights over three decades of experience in the decorated-apparel and promotional-products market.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Screen printing", "Embroidery", "Appliqu\u00e9", "Promotional products sourcing and decoration", "Graphic design and branding", "Private label manufacturing", "Corporate fulfillment", "Banners and signs"], "industries": ["Ski resorts", "Golf resorts", "Country clubs", "Corporate events and employee recognition", "Trade shows and promotional giveaways"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house art department works directly with production for quality control", "In-house screen printing and embroidery/appliqu\u00e9 facilities", "Reduced lead times through internal production", "Private-label manufacturing for resort and golf apparel"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1985 -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Salt Lake City, Utah -> db", "Began designing sportswear for ski resorts in Colorado, California, Utah -> /about-us", "Expanded to golf resorts and country clubs in USA and Canada -> /about-us", "Offers screen printing, embroidery, promotional products, art and branding -> /services, /", "In-house art department, screen print facility, embroidery/appliqu\u00e9 services -> /about-us, /", "Produces SDI Resort and Golf sportswear and private label brands -> /about-us", "In-house production reduces lead times and improves quality control -> /services", "Designers work closely with production for quality control -> /services", "Corporate customers use for events and employee recognition -> /about-us", "Over 30 years industry experience -> /", "Corporate fulfillment, banners & signs -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We produce SDI Resort and Golf sportswear and design and manufacture private label brands.", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sdi-printex' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sea Fresh USA, Inc. was founded in 1981 in North Kingstown, Rhode Island. The company began as a shoreside partner for seafood brands and has since grown into a vertically integrated processor of wild-caught squid and finfish. In 2023, it joined the American Seafood Partners family of brands, expanding its access to vessels, docks, and raw materials.

The company manages the full supply chain from fishing through packing at its BRC-certified facility in North Kingstown. Its dedicated fleet unloads at the Port of Galilee in Narragansett, providing access to a significant portion of Northeast seafood landings. The plant operates year-round, cleaning squid by hand to customer specifications using both blast and contact freezers. Flagship items include Boston Loligo (Doryteuthis pealeii) and Boston Illex (Illex illecebrosus), alongside imported squid species and local finfish.

Sea Fresh serves major house brands, global foodservice distributors, and restaurant chains through private-label and co-packing partnerships. Its private-label expertise spans decades, with the facility packing custom-branded cases for white-label customers across retail and foodservice channels.

The company differentiates itself through vertical integration, MSC-certified sustainable squid, and strict BRC food safety compliance. It emphasizes traceable chain-of-custody and brand protection, positioning its locally caught, locally processed calamari as a premium product for chefs and culinary professionals.', certifications=ARRAY['BRC','MSC']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Squid cleaning and processing", "Private label packing", "Co-packing", "Blast freezing", "Contact freezing", "Vertical integration (fishing, unloading, processing, packing)", "MSC chain of custody", "BRC food safety compliance"], "industries": ["Foodservice distribution", "Restaurant chains", "Retail private label", "Seafood processing"], "materials": ["Boston Loligo squid (Doryteuthis pealeii)", "Boston Illex squid (Illex illecebrosus)", "Imported squid species", "Northeast fin fish"], "equipment": ["Blast freezers", "Contact freezers"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated from fishing to packing", "BRC-certified processing facility", "MSC-certified sustainable Northeast longfin inshore squid", "Dedicated fleet and dock access at Port of Galilee", "Hand-cleaned squid to exact customer specifications"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1981 -> /about-us", "Headquarters in North Kingstown, Rhode Island -> db", "Vertically integrated: fishing, unloading, processing, packing in-house -> /about-us", "Joined American Seafood Partners family of brands in 2023 -> /about-us", "Dedicated fleet unloads at Port of Galilee, Narragansett, RI -> /about-us", "BRC-certified facility in North Kingstown -> /about-us", "Blast and contact freezers -> /about-us", "Flagship product: Boston Loligo (Doryteuthis pealeii) -> /about-us", "Also processes Boston Illex (Illex illecebrosus), imported squid, local finfish -> /about-us", "Serves major house brands, global foodservice distributors, restaurant chains -> /", "Private label expertise for decades -> /", "MSC certified sustainable for Northeast U.S. Longfin Inshore Squid -> /", "BRC Certified Facility -> /", "Private Label Expertise -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We do not just package seafood; we manage the entire process from the Atlantic Ocean to your custom-branded case.", "founded_year": "1981", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sea-fresh-usa-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Seastrom Manufacturing Co. Inc. was founded in 1928 in Twin Falls, Idaho. The company began as a manufacturer of precision washers and assembly hardware and has since grown into a full-service washer manufacturer and supplier operating under the Seastrom family of companies, which includes Seastrom Stamping and Acacia Machining.

The company produces precision washers, military hardware, and custom assembly hardware. It operates precision stamping, CNC machining (including 7-axis Swiss CNC with 10,000 rpm spindle), compound and progressive stamping, four-slide stamping, multi-spindle screw machining, and waterjet cutting. It stocks over 60,000 part numbers and offers in-house tool and die, custom packaging, labeling, barcoding, and kitting. The company claims to stock the largest quantity of precision fasteners in the industry, with over 44,000 part numbers.

Seastrom serves aerospace, defense, electronics, communications, energy, medical, agriculture, machinery, and firearms industries. It is an approved supplier for major aerospace and commercial manufacturers.

The company emphasizes short lead times, with most stocked products delivered within 48 hours, and highlights its U.S.-based manufacturing and long history of custom-to-print parts since 1928. It also offers custom engineering to enable manufacturing of new parts to exact specifications.', certifications=ARRAY['ANSI']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision stamping", "Precision CNC machining", "Compound and progressive stamping", "Four-slide stamping", "Multi-spindle screw machining", "Swiss CNC machining (7-axis)", "Waterjet cutting", "Custom packaging (static-resistant, custom labeling, barcoding, kitting)", "In-house tool and die", "Custom engineering", "Custom to print manufacturing"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Electronics", "Communications", "Energy", "Medical", "Agriculture", "Machinery", "Firearms"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "48 hours for stocked products", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 60,000 standard part numbers in stock", "Most stocked products delivered within 48 hours", "Custom-to-print parts since 1928", "Approved supplier for major aerospace and commercial manufacturers", "In-house tool and die department"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1928 -> /", "Headquarters Twin Falls, Idaho -> db", "Over 60,000 part numbers stocked -> /", "48-hour delivery for stocked products -> /", "Custom-to-print since 1928 -> /", "Approved supplier for major aerospace and commercial manufacturers -> /", "In-house tool and die -> /", "Capabilities: precision stamping, CNC machining, compound/progressive stamping, four-slide, multi-spindle screw machining, Swiss CNC 7-axis, waterjet cutting -> /", "Industries served: aerospace, defense, electronics, communications, energy, medical, agriculture, machinery, firearms -> /", "Certifications: ANSI -> db", "Subsidiaries: Seastrom Stamping, Acacia Machining -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Seastrom is the Premier Manufacturer of Precision Washers and Precision Assembly Hardware.", "founded_year": "1928", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='seastrom-manufacturing-co-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sechan Electronics is headquartered in Lititz, Pennsylvania. The company operates as a 100% employee-owned business through an ESOP structure. No founding year or founders are disclosed in public materials.

The firm provides electronic contract manufacturing services focused on defense applications. Its production capabilities include circuit card assembly, wiring harness fabrication, and end-item integration, supported by automated through-hole component insertion equipment. Sechan also offers electrical, environmental, and EMI/EMC testing, along with design services governed by CMMI Level 3 and ISO 9000 procedures covering project planning, inventory control, integration, verification, and validation.

Sechan serves the U.S. Department of Defense and its prime contractors exclusively. Customer references include the U.S. Air Force, Army, Navy, and Marine Corps, as well as major primes such as BAE Systems, Boeing, Draper Laboratory, Johnson Controls, L3Harris Technologies, Lockheed Martin, Northrop Grumman, Raytheon Technologies, Sierra Nevada Corporation, Textron Systems, and Ultra Electronics.

The company emphasizes three differentiators: it is solely dedicated to DoD work, it positions itself as solution-driven with engineering-heavy support for troubleshooting and circuit analysis, and its employee-ownership model aims to align incentives with customer success. Additional distinguishing factors include resident DCMA personnel, extensive product and data security experience, and high-reliability engineering expertise.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Circuit card assembly", "Wiring harness assembly", "End item integration", "Electrical testing", "Environmental testing", "EMI/EMC testing (MIL-STD-461/462)", "Design services (CMMI Level 3, ISO 9000)", "Project planning", "Inventory control", "Integration", "Verification and validation", "Automated through-hole component insertion", "High-density multi-layered design", "Thermal management", "Precise component bonding"], "industries": ["Defense", "Aerospace", "Military"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Automated through-hole component insertion equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% dedicated to Department of Defense contracts", "100% solution-driven with engineering-heavy support", "100% employee-owned (ESOP)", "Resident DCMA personnel on site", "Extensive product and data security experience"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Lititz, PA -> db", "Employee-owned ESOP -> /", "Electronic contract manufacturing services -> /", "Circuit card assembly, wiring harness, end item integration -> /", "Electrical, environmental, EMI/EMC testing -> /", "Design services with CMMI Level 3 and ISO 9000 -> /", "Customers: U.S. Air Force, Army, Navy, Marines, BAE Systems, Boeing, Draper Laboratory, Johnson Controls, L3Harris, Lockheed Martin, Northrop Grumman, Raytheon, Sierra Nevada, Textron, Ultra Electronics -> /", "100% dedicated to DoD, solution-driven, employee-owned -> /", "Resident DCMA personnel -> /", "AS9100 certification -> db", "Automated through-hole component insertion equipment -> /", "Small Business Classification -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Sechan Electronics is committed to the development, testing and manufacturing of military defense electronics systems and subsystems for the Department of Defense and Prime Contractors.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sechan-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sekisui Kasei USA Inc. operates its Tennessee plant in Mt. Pleasant, part of a global polymer and foam specialist founded in Japan in 1959. The U.S. subsidiary of Sekisui Kasei Co., Ltd. maintains four North American locations among 36 worldwide, with the Mt. Pleasant facility serving as headquarters for its American operations.

The company develops and manufactures polymer materials and finished foam parts using polymerization, extrusion, molding, and foaming technologies. Its product portfolio includes EPS and Piocelan molded foams for automotive lightweighting and impact absorption, ST Gels for healthcare fastening and sensing applications, and Techpolymer spherical polymer particles used as additives in cosmetics, coatings, and films. Custom foam packaging solutions are designed for automotive components, heavy transmissions, and sheet metal parts.

Primary markets include automotive OEMs and tier suppliers seeking lightweight, high-impact absorption parts and transportation packaging for interior, exterior, and heavy components.

Sekisui Kasei emphasizes a collaborative design engineering approach, working directly with customers to develop protective solutions that leverage six decades of foaming technology expertise. Its differentiation rests on unique ion cross-link chemistry, proprietary polymerization for spherical particles, and accumulated logistics data that optimizes packaging density and reduces shipping costs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Polymerization", "Extrusion", "Molding", "Foaming", "Ion cross-link technology", "ST Gels production", "Techpolymer production", "Custom foam packaging design", "Automotive parts transportation packaging design", "Lightweight high-impact absorption parts manufacturing", "Cosmetic additive formulation", "Anti-blocking agent production"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Healthcare", "Medical", "Cosmetics", "Home Appliances", "Information Technology", "Industrial"], "materials": ["EPS", "Piocelan", "ST Gels", "Techpolymer", "Styrene", "Methyl Methacrylate", "Ion cross-link polymers", "Foam materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1959 in Japan -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Mt. Pleasant, Tennessee -> /", "36 global locations, 4 in North America -> /about-us", "Subsidiary of Sekisui Kasei Co., Ltd. -> /about-us", "Processes: polymerization, extrusion, molding, foaming -> /", "Products: EPS, Piocelan, ST Gels, Techpolymer -> /", "Industries: automotive, healthcare, medical, cosmetic, home appliances, information technology -> /", "Collaborative design engineering approach -> /about-us", "President: Michelle Williams -> /about-us", "Unique ion cross-link technology -> /", "Techpolymer based on styrene and methyl methacrylate -> /", "Custom foam packaging for automotive parts -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Sekisui Kasei U.S.A. Inc., a subsidiary of Sekisui Kasei Co., Ltd., is a leading provider of polymer materials and finished foam parts.", "founded_year": "1959", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sekisui-kasei-usa-inc-tennessee-plant' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SemiPack Services Inc operates from West Melbourne, Florida, where it has served the semiconductor and electronics manufacturing sectors for over a decade. The company was founded to provide specialized electronic manufacturing support services, though the exact founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The company focuses on four core service lines: BGA reballing and restoration, tape and reel packaging, robotic tinning, and trim and form lead processing. Its tape and reel operation maintains an inventory of more than 4,000 component pockets, including hard-to-find configurations, and supports both manual and automated processing. Additional capabilities include XRF material composition testing, product testing, baking, dry packing, and custom pocket design and tooling. SemiPack positions itself as a high-mix low-volume (HMLV) specialist.

Customers span the semiconductor industry, electronics manufacturers, and aerospace and defense contractors. The company''s ITAR registration and compliance with GEIA-0006 and IEC TS 62647-4 make it a qualified supplier for defense-related programs. It also serves RoHS-compliant manufacturers requiring tin-lead conversions for legacy processes.

SemiPack emphasizes its large pocket inventory, rapid turnaround on non-standard pockets, and adherence to military and aerospace specifications as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ITAR','GEIA-0006','IEC TS 62647-4','RoHS compliance']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["BGA reballing", "BGA restoration", "Tape and reel packaging", "Robotic tinning", "Trim and form", "Lead forming", "XRF testing", "Product testing", "Custom pocket design and tooling", "Baking and dry packing", "Manual and automated processing"], "industries": ["Semiconductor", "Electronics manufacturing", "Aerospace", "Defense"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "High-mix low-volume (HMLV)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Inventory of over 4,000 tape-and-reel pockets, including hard-to-find component pockets", "GEIA-0006 and IEC TS 62647-4 compliant for BGA restoration", "Robotic tinning services for RoHS-to-SnPb and SnPb-to-RoHS conversions", "BGA reballing and restoration with speed and reliability for high-mix low-volume orders"], "facts_used": ["Company name, location, certifications, capabilities, industries served -> db", "Headquarters city and state -> db", "Services: BGA reballing, tape & reel, robotic tinning, trim & form -> db and /", "Compliance: GEIA-0006, IEC TS 62647-4, ITAR, AS9100D, ISO 9001:2015 -> /", "Inventory of over 4,000 pockets -> /", "High-mix low-volume (HMLV) focus -> /", "XRF services for aerospace and defense -> /", "RoHS and SnPb conversions -> /", "Custom pocket design and tooling -> /", "Baking and dry packing services -> /", "Product testing services -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "SemiPack Services is an Electronic Manufacturing Support Service to the semiconductor industry.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='semipack-services-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Semiconductor Hybrid Assembly, Inc. (SHA) was founded in 1988 by Yassin Burgol in Wixom, Michigan. The family-owned business began with Ford Motor Company as its first customer, serving the metro Detroit area from an 800-square-foot building. Burgol was later joined by his wife Eva and sons Hisham and Ayman, and today three generations of the family operate the company.

SHA provides printed circuit board assembly services including surface-mount (SMT) and through-hole assembly, harness and test-box fabrication, conformal coating, electrical testing, rework, repair, and X-ray parts counting. The company operates a 16,000-square-foot facility with over 20 employees whose combined experience exceeds 400 years. Equipment includes Samsung SMD pick-and-place machines capable of 01005 and complex BGA placement, wave and selective soldering systems, automated optical inspection, 2D X-ray inspection, BGA rework stations, and an Aquastorm PCB wash system.

The shop serves original equipment manufacturers, Tier 1 and Tier 2 automotive suppliers, aftermarket companies, startups, and environmental-sector clients. Its assemblies are used in applications such as vehicle-to-everything (V2X) and vehicle-to-vehicle (V2V) communication systems. Customers range from global OEMs to small businesses seeking rapid prototypes or low-volume production.

