UPDATE companies SET description='Sheet Metal Contracting Company, Inc. traces its roots to 1910 when Ruben I. Hutt opened an inventor’s shop at 218½ French Street in Wilmington, Delaware. The family-owned business moved to its current 24,000‑square‑foot facility on Wrangle Hill Road in Bear in 1978 after Hutt sold the operation to Bob Bupp and Howard Banning. Today the company is led by owner Jeff Bupp and a small team of fabrication specialists.

The shop provides custom metal fabrication — CNC cutting, bending, punching, machining, and welding — for projects ranging from single prototypes to runs of thousands of parts. Its equipment lineup handles materials from standard hot‑rolled steel through rare alloys and stainless grades, as well as plastics. The facility sits along the I‑95 corridor, allowing quick access to Delaware, Maryland, Pennsylvania, and New Jersey.

Core markets include the chemical, energy, textile, and agriculture sectors. Long‑standing customers include DuPont, W.L. Gore, and Siemens, alongside regional machine shops and contractors. Finished work ships throughout North America and overseas.

The company emphasizes fabrication expertise honed over more than a century, offering design and engineering assistance to meet exact specifications with swift turnaround times.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC cutting", "CNC bending", "CNC punching", "Machining", "Welding", "Custom metal fabrication", "Design/engineering assistance"], "industries": ["Chemical", "Energy", "Textile", "Agriculture"], "materials": ["Hot rolled steel", "Alloy steels", "Stainless steel", "Plastics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to thousands of parts", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned since 1910", "24,000 sq ft facility on I\u201195 corridor", "Prototype to production volumes", "Works with rare alloys, stainless, and plastics", "Design/engineering assistance and swift turnaround"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1910 by Ruben I. Hutt in Wilmington, DE -> /about", "Relocated to Bear, DE in 1978 after sale to Bob Bupp and Howard Banning -> /about", "Currently operated by owner Jeff Bupp -> /about", "Family-owned business -> /about", "24,000 sq ft facility at 3445 Wrangle Hill Road, Bear, DE -> /about", "Capabilities: CNC cut, bend, punch, machine, weld -> /", "Projects from one-item prototype to hundreds or thousands of parts -> /", "Materials: hot rolled steels, rare alloys, stainless steels, plastics -> /about", "Industries served: chemical, energy, textile, agriculture -> /about", "Customers include DuPont, W.L. Gore, Siemens -> /about", "Also serves other metal/machine shops and contractors -> /about", "Located along I-95 corridor serving DE, MD, PA, NJ; work worldwide -> /about", "Offers design/engineering assistance and swift turnaround times -> /about", "Headquarters in Bear, Delaware -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "custom metal fabrication company that manufacturers primarily for the industrial and commercial fields", "founded_year": "1910", "em