UPDATE companies SET description='Sheet Metal Werks, Inc. operates from Arlington Heights, Illinois, in the Chicago metropolitan area. The company was founded in 1987 by Kevin Ryan and his father, who began fabricating sheet metal in a Des Plaines shop while Kevin and his wife Sue managed operations from their kitchen table. The Ryans remain at the helm today, with Kevin as chief executive and Sue as chief financial officer, making the business a family-owned enterprise.

The firm specializes in custom high-efficiency HVAC sheet metal systems, including rectangular and spiral ductwork, fittings, and polyvinyl (PVS) exhaust systems. It also fabricates pre-insulated Thermaduct and Kingspan KoolDuct phenolic foam systems for applications requiring high R-values and low air leakage. Equipment includes a computer-guided plasma cutter capable of 10- to 26-gauge stock and a new Pro-Fabriduct coil line from Iowa Precision that the company says reduces air leakage by up to 40 percent. The shop handles projects ranging from standard spiral pipe to fully welded custom assemblies.

Sheet Metal Werks serves commercial, industrial, healthcare, education, and government construction markets. Notable projects include ductwork for Macy’s State Street flagship in Chicago, the Goodman Theatre, and a government facility that adopted Thermaduct for indoor-air-quality improvements. Its customer base consists largely of mechanical and HVAC contractors such as Amco Inc., CT Mechanical, Energy Matters, Hartwig Mechanical, and Sun Mechanical Systems. The company also provides preconstruction estimating from bid-set or BIM-coordinated drawings.

The business was built on a “never say no to work” philosophy inherited from Kevin’s father, and it maintains a union workforce. Management emphasizes on-time delivery from indoor loading docks, nationwide shipping at competitive rates, and a one-stop-shop approach that includes a full line of HVAC accessories.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Commercial/Industrial sheet metal fabrication", "Thermaduct fabrication", "KoolDuct fabrication", "Rectangular duct and fittings fabrication", "Spiral pipe and fittings fabrication", "Low pressure pipe and fittings fabrication", "HVAC accessories supply", "Preconstruction estimating (bid-set and BIM)", "Computer-guided plasma cutting", "Welding of custom assemblies", "Coil line processing (Pro-Fabriduct)", "Design and fabrication from start to finish"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Industrial construction", "Healthcare facilities", "Assisted living", "Education (schools)", "Government facilities", "HVAC/mechanical contractors"], "materials": ["Galvanized steel", "Stainless steel", "Black iron", "Aluminum", "PVC-coated steel", "Paint grip steel", "Phenolic foam (Kingspan KoolDuct)", "Polyvinyl (PVS) duct"], "equipment": ["Computer-guided plasma cutter", "Pro-Fabriduct coil line (Iowa Precision)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "2 days for stocked items (per customer testimonial)", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Union shop with made-in-USA products", "Computer-guided plasma cutter for custom ductwork in 10- to 26-gauge stock", "Pro-Fabriduct coil line reducing air leakage up to 40%", "Indoor docks protecting finished product during loading", "Preconstruction estimating from bid-set and BIM-coordinated drawings"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1987 -> db, /, /about", "Headquarters Arlington Heights, Illinois -> db", "Facility size 80,000 sq ft -> /", "Facility size 150,000 sq ft after redesign -> /about, /services", "Employees nearly 80 -> /about", "Founders Kevin Ryan and his father -> /about",