UPDATE companies SET description='Shiloh Custom Molding operates from Paris, Arkansas, where it was founded in 1996. The company is family-owned and operated by four partners, including three brothers—Seth, John, and Jesse Green—alongside William Heffington. The business began with a focus on rotational molding and has grown to offer full-service solutions from production to fulfillment.

The company runs two rotational molding machines to produce hollow plastic parts such as tanks, enclosures, bins, housings, and custom components. In addition to molding, Shiloh provides in-house finishing services for surface texture control and operates a drop-ship fulfillment program that stores finished parts and ships directly to end customers. The firm coordinates mold fabrication with partners and maintains molds in-house to ensure consistent quality. Production runs are flexible, accommodating prototype batches through large-scale orders.

Shiloh serves a range of industries including automotive, industrial equipment, medical and dental, consumer products, agriculture, marine, construction, and electronics.

The partners emphasize a hands-on, family-owned approach that prioritizes craftsmanship, responsive service, and low overhead to keep pricing competitive. They cite in-house texture control, drop-ship logistics, and efficient production planning as key differentiators that allow them to deliver consistent quality and reliable turnaround.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Rotational molding", "Finishing services (surface texture control)", "Drop-ship fulfillment", "Mold maintenance coordination", "Part design review and optimization", "Inventory storage and management"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Industrial Equipment", "Medical & Dental", "Consumer Products", "Agriculture", "Marine", "Construction", "Electronics"], "materials": ["Polyethylene"], "equipment": ["Two rotational molding machines"], "volume": "Small prototype batches to large-scale orders", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned, hands-on management", "In-house surface texture control", "Drop-ship fulfillment from on-site inventory", "Low overhead for competitive pricing", "Efficient production planning and reliable turnaround"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 -> db", "Headquarters Paris, Arkansas -> db", "Family-owned, partners Seth Green, John Green, Jesse Green, William Heffington -> /about-us", "Two rotational molding machines -> /about-us", "Rotational molding, finishing, drop ship fulfillment -> /", "Industries served: automotive, industrial equipment, medical & dental, consumer products, agriculture, marine, construction, electronics -> /", "Materials: polyethylene -> /", "Clients: Terracast Products, Mullet Tools, Shure-Step -> /", "Flexible production runs from prototype to large-scale -> /", "In-house texture control -> /about-us", "Mold maintenance coordination -> /about-us", "Part design review and feedback -> /about-us", "Inventory storage and direct-to-customer shipping -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Shiloh Custom Molding is a family-owned rotational molding company", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='shiloh-custom-molding' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Short Circuit Electronics was founded in 1994 by Thomas Wright in Staunton, Virginia. The shop remains family-owned, operated by Thomas and his wife Jami Wright. Thomas, a professional sound engineer who also serves as audio engineer for Village Church in Churchville, opened the business with a simple goal: do great work and treat every customer like a neighbor.

The company provides installation, repair, and custom integration services for automotive, marine, powersports, residential, and commercial electronics. Core services include car audio system design and installation (head units, speakers, subwoofers, amplifiers), 3M window tint and security film application, remote start and alarm systems (Viper, Avital), custom LED lighting, home theater and whole-home audio, commercial audio/video for churches, restaurants, and venues, security camera and alarm systems, and general electronics repair such as wiring harness and instrument cluster diagnostics. The shop handles projects ranging from daily-driver upgrades to fleet vehicles, vintage restorations, and one-off custom builds.

Customers span individual vehicle owners, motorcycle and UTV enthusiasts, boat owners, homeowners seeking theater installations, and commercial clients including churches, restaurants, sports bars, and fleet operators. The team regularly works on cars, trucks, motorcycles, boats, UTVs, golf carts, and has experience with emergency vehicle lighting and vintage electronics restoration.

The Wrights attribute their longevity to Thomas’s professional acoustics expertise, over three decades of hands-on experience, a willingness to tackle unusual or difficult projects other shops decline, and a community-first mindset that emphasizes honest advice and quality workmanship over upselling.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Car audio system design and consultation", "Head unit / stereo installation", "Speaker upgrade and custom installation", "Subwoofer and enclosure installation", "Amplifier installation and tuning", "Marine and powersports audio installation", "3M window tint and security film installation", "Heat and UV reduction film application", "Security film for doors and storefronts", "Remote start system installation (one-way, two-way, smartphone integration)", "Car alarm system installation (shock sensors, glass break, tilt detection, GPS tracking)", "Custom LED lighting installation (interior accent, underbody, wheel well, headlight/taillight upgrades)", "Smartphone-controlled lighting systems", "Home theater installation (TV mounting, surround sound, speaker placement, receiver/amplifier setup)", "Whole-home audio solutions", "Outdoor audio system installation", "Commercial audio/video installation (church/worship, restaurant/bar, event venue, conference room AV)", "Commercial TV installation", "Security camera system installation", "Video doorbell and motion detection setup", "Home and commercial alarm system installation", "Remote monitoring setup", "Electronics repair (instrument cluster, wiring harness, electrical diagnostics, audio troubleshooting)", "Backup camera and dash camera installation and repair"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Marine", "Motorcycle", "Powersports", "Commercial", "Fleet", "Home Theater", "Vintage Restoration"], "materials": ["3M window film"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Professional sound engineer on staff (Thomas Wright)", "32+ years