UPDATE companies SET description='Silicon Ranch Corporation, headquartered in Nashville, Tennessee, began operations in 2011 with two employees. The company pioneered utility-scale solar development in the Southeast, commissioning the first such projects in Tennessee, Georgia, Mississippi, Arkansas, and Kentucky.

The firm develops, owns, and operates utility-scale solar and battery storage projects across 15 states, with more than 4,000 megawatts in operation and over 5 gigawatts contracted. Its integrated model covers planning, construction, operations, and eventual decommissioning. In addition to power generation, Silicon Ranch runs a regenerative land management program that grazes more than 2,000 sheep and cattle on project sites, supported by a proprietary CattleTracker™ system and a 26,000-square-foot lambing barn at the Houston Solar Project.

Customers include electric utilities and cooperatives such as BrightRidge and Georgia Power, commercial and industrial partners like Volkswagen and Aerojet Rocketdyne, and landowners who lease acreage for solar farms. The company also serves corporate buyers through Clearloop, a subsidiary that sells carbon reclamation tied to new solar construction.

Silicon Ranch differentiates itself by retaining long-term ownership of every project, a record of delivering every power purchase agreement since inception, and a focus on restoring soil health and biodiversity through agrivoltaics. Partnerships with SOLARCYCLE for module recycling and with First Solar and Nextracker for domestic equipment sourcing further underscore its supply-chain commitments.', certifications=ARRAY['Savory Institute regenerative land certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Utility-scale solar project development", "Solar project ownership and operation", "Battery storage integration", "Carbon reclamation solutions (Clearloop)", "Regenerative land management (agrivoltaics)", "Sheep grazing for vegetation control", "Cattle grazing integration (CattleTracker\u2122)", "Solar module recycling (via SOLARCYCLE partnership)", "Project planning, construction, operations, decommissioning", "Domestic solar equipment procurement (First Solar, Nextracker)"], "industries": ["Utility-scale solar energy", "Electric utilities and cooperatives", "Commercial and industrial energy procurement", "Agrivoltaics and regenerative agriculture", "Carbon offset and reclamation", "Solar equipment recycling"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["First Solar photovoltaic modules", "Nextracker solar tracking systems", "CattleTracker\u2122 monitoring system", "Swap Robotics (investment)", "Lambing barn (26,000 sq ft)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Owns and operates every project for its full life", "Delivered every signed power purchase agreement since 2011", "First utility-scale solar in five southeastern states", "Regenerative Energy\u00ae program with company-owned livestock and CattleTracker\u2122 technology", "Partnership with SOLARCYCLE for end-of-life solar module recycling"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Nashville, Tennessee -> db", "Founded 2011, began with two employees -> /about", "180+ projects across 15 states, 4,000+