UPDATE companies SET description='SisTech Manufacturing operates from a purpose-built facility in Bend, Oregon. The company was founded by industry veterans with deep experience in electronics manufacturing, though a specific founding year is not disclosed. The leadership team includes CEO Brad Kennedy, formerly VP of Operations at Vadatech Inc. and General Manager at GE Fanuc Embedded Systems Group; Operations lead Tyler Eggleston, with background at Raytheon and Collins Aerospace; and Supply Chain manager Mike Greer, a 30-year veteran of Arrow Electronics.

SisTech provides contract electronic manufacturing and mechanical assembly services, specializing in turnkey and kitted printed circuit board assemblies from quick-turn prototypes to high-volume production. Its capabilities include surface-mount placement down to 01005 components, BGA/microBGA/LGA/CSP/PoP assembly, selective soldering, in-house conformal coating, and a full suite of testing — automated optical inspection (2D/3D), X-ray with CT scan, functional and in-circuit test. The Bend facility houses six Europlacer SMT lines, Mirtec AOI, Nordson DAGE X-ray, ERSA and Aqueous Tech equipment. The company also offers design-for-manufacturing feedback, PCB layout support, obsolescence management, box-build integration, and a counterfeit-parts prevention program.

The company serves high-technology customers in defense, aerospace, energy, embedded electronics, and consumer electronics across the Pacific Northwest and nationally. It targets partners with mid- to high-range production volumes, defined production roadmaps, and requirements for rigorous quality, documentation, and traceability — explicitly avoiding one-off prototypes with no production intent and ultra-high-volume commodity builds.

SisTech differentiates itself through a lifetime manufacturing warranty, proactive DFM engagement, and a partnership model that includes early component procurement against customer forecasts. Its quality system is certified to ISO 9001:2015, ITAR registered, and CMMC Level 1, with staff certified to IPC-A-610 and IPC-7711/7721. The leadership team’s collective 130-plus years of experience underpins a focus on complex, high-reliability assemblies and long-term supply-chain stability.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ITAR Registered','CMMC Level 1','IPC-A-610','IPC-7711/7721']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Turnkey PCB Assembly", "Kitted PCB Assembly", "Rapid Prototyping", "High-Volume Production", "Surface Mount Technology (SMT) Assembly", "Through-Hole Assembly", "01005 Component Placement", "BGA / microBGA / LGA / CSP / PoP Assembly", "Selective Soldering", "Conformal Coating", "Automated Optical Inspection (2D/3D)", "X-Ray Inspection (with CT Scan)", "Functional Testing", "In-Circuit Testing", "JTAG Testing", "Design for Manufacturing (DFM) Feedback", "PCB Layout Support", "Obsolescence Part Management", "Box Build Assembly", "Component Procurement & Supply Chain Management", "Counterfeit Parts Prevention", "Drop Shipping", "Lot Tracking & Traceability", "Early Component Procurement (forecast-driven)"], "industries": ["Defense", "Aerospace", "Energy", "Embedded Electronics", "Consumer Electronics", "Commercial", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Europlacer SMT Machines (6)", "Mirtec 2D/3D Automated Optical Inspection", "Nordson DAGE X-Ray with X-Plane CT Scan", "ERSA Selective Soldering", "Aqueous Tech Cleaning Systems", "In-Circuit Test Equipment", "Functional Test Equipment"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "72 hours for rapid prototypes (with complete validated data package)", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lifetime manufacturing warranty on workmanship", "72-hour rapid prototyping turnaround for validated data packages", "In-house conformal coating and full testing suite (AOI, X-ray CT, functional, in-circuit)", "Proactive DFM feedback and obsolescence management program", "ITAR registered, CMMC Level 1, ISO 9001:2015 certified with IPC-certified staff"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Bend, Oregon -> /about-us", "Founded by industry veterans -> /about-us", "Leadership team: Brad Kennedy, Tyler Eggleston, Mike Greer -> /about-us", "ISO 9001:2015 certified, ITAR registered, CMMC Level 1 certified -> / and /about-us", "130+ years combined experience -> /about-us", "6 Europlacer SMT machines -> /", "Mirtec 2D/3D AOI, Nordson DAGE X-ray -> /", "Complex assemblies: 01005 placement, BGA, microBGA, LGA, CSP, PoP -> /", "Industries served: defense, aerospace, energy, embedded electronics, consumer electronics -> /about-us", "Rapid prototyping in 72 hours -> /services", "Turnkey & kitted PCB assemblies -> /services", "In-house conformal coating -> /services", "DFM feedback and PCB layout support -> /services", "Obsolescence management -> /services", "Box build assembly -> /services", "Lifetime manufacturing warranty -> / and /about-us", "Counterfeit parts prevention program -> /about-us", "Facility address: 63068 Lower Meadow Drive, Bend, OR 97701 -> /about-us", "ERSA, Aqueous Tech equipment -> /", "IPC-A-610 and IPC-7711/7721 certified employees -> / and /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "SisTech Manufacturing, based in Bend, Oregon, provides contract electronic manufacturing and mechanical assembly services to high-technology companies across the Pacific Northwest and beyond.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sistech-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Six Six Apparel operates from Brownsburg, Indiana, just west of Indianapolis. The business began in 2006 as a home-based screen printing shop run out of a garage, where screens were washed at a local carwash. After moving through several garage spaces, the company settled into its current facility in 2017.

The shop provides custom screen printing, dye sublimation printing, direct-to-film (DTF) printing, embroidery, graphic design, and cut-and-sew manufacturing. It produces over 200,000 screen printed shirts annually and runs a cut-and-sew team that assembles dye-sublimated garments with edge-to-edge graphics. The facility handles all-over sublimation on performance fabrics such as dry-fit, moisture-wicking, and UV-protective materials, and uses eco-friendly inks with Pantone color matching.

Customers span athletic activewear, hospitality, motorsports, and corporate apparel. The company has produced dye-sublimated jerseys, uniforms, and hoodies for racing teams, bowling leagues, professional fishing apparel, clay shooting teams, and archery leagues. It also supplies embroidered corporate wear—polos, jackets, hats, bags, and luggage—and prints banners, flags, and table covers for hospitality events.

